\details{
\subsection{Scaling from per-recruit to absolute}{

All F-dependent slots are obtained by multiplying the corresponding
per-recruit quantity from a \link[=perrecruit-class]{perrecruit} object by equilibrium
recruitment:
\deqn{\texttt{Recruits}_{s,F} = R_{0,s} \cdot \phi(\texttt{SPR}_{s,F})}
where \eqn{\phi} is the relative recruitment function from the stock's
\code{\link[=SRR]{SRR()}} and \eqn{R_{0,s}} is unfished recruitment. Values of
\code{RelRecruits} below zero are floored at zero before scaling.
}

\subsection{Complexes}{

When stocks belong to the same complex they share a single apical F, and
\code{SPR} for each stock is computed relative to that complex-level F. The
\code{RelRecruits} scaling is still applied per stock.
}
}
